# Salesforce Record-Triggered Flow Automation

Record-Triggered Flows are used to automate business processes whenever a record is created or updated. These flows eliminate manual work and ensure data consistency.

---

## Flow 1 – Set Application Date Automatically

**Flow Category:** Before-Save Record-Triggered Flow

**Object:** Application__c

**Execution:** When a new Application record is created.

**Functionality:**
The flow automatically assigns the current date to the **Application Date** field, ensuring every application has a valid submission date without manual entry.

---

## Flow 2 – Placement Officer Email Notification

**Flow Category:** After-Save Record-Triggered Flow

**Object:** Application__c

**Execution:** When a new Application record is successfully created.

**Functionality:**
An email notification is automatically sent to the Placement Officer informing them that a new placement application has been submitted.

---

## Flow 3 – Automatic Offer Letter Generation

**Flow Category:** After-Save Record-Triggered Flow

**Object:** Application__c

**Execution:** When an existing Application record is updated and the **Status** changes to **Selected**.

**Functionality:**
The flow creates a new **Offer Letter** record and links it to the corresponding Application, Student, and Job records whenever a candidate is selected.
